"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Twisted Image","oracle_id":"4a40cee1-fc09-4f97-aef8-440778d8c0ca","oracle_text":"Switch target creature's power and toughness until end of turn.\nDraw a card.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2018-03-16","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Flying"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{U}","name":"Wind Drake","oracle_id":"d6ffdaf0-ac08-4de9-bbce-2eab2f86bcca","oracle_text":"Flying","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2016-09-30","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature — Drake"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["R"],"colors":["R"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Split second"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{3}{R}{R}","name":"Word of Seizing","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","oracle_text":"Split second (As long as this spell is on the stack, players can't cast spells or activate abilities that aren't mana abilities.)\nUntap target permanent and gain control of it until end of turn. It gains haste until end of turn.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-11-20","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Effects that modify a creature’s power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Overprotect, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch its power and toughness.","oracle_id":"129476ae-9dab-4e04-8e8e-f249afd56ff9","published_at":"2024-07-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Maha’s last ability overwrites all previous effects that set those creatures’ base toughness to specific values. Any toughness-setting effects that start to apply afterward will overwrite this effect.","oracle_id":"129476ae-9dab-4e04-8e8e-f249afd56ff9","published_at":"2024-07-26","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Because damage remains marked on a creature until the damage is removed as the turn ends, nonlethal damage dealt to a creature may become lethal if you switch its power and toughness during that turn.","oracle_id":"4a40cee1-fc09-4f97-aef8-440778d8c0ca","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Effects that switch a creature's power and toughness apply after all other effects, regardless of when those effects began to apply. For instance, if you target a 1/2 creature then give it +2/+0 later in the turn, it's a 2/3 creature, not a 4/1 creature.","oracle_id":"4a40cee1-fc09-4f97-aef8-440778d8c0ca","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Switching a creature's power and toughness twice (or any even number of times) effectively returns the creature to the power and toughness it had before any switches.","oracle_id":"4a40cee1-fc09-4f97-aef8-440778d8c0ca","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"After a spell with split second resolves (or otherwise leaves the stack), players may again cast spells and activate abilities before the next object on the stack resolves.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Casting a spell with split second won't affect spells and abilities that are already on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the resolution of a triggered ability involves casting a spell, that spell can't be cast if a spell with split second is on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Players may turn face-down creatures face up while a spell with split second is on the stack.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Players still get priority while a card with split second is on the stack; their options are just limited to mana abilities and certain special actions.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Split second doesn't stop triggered abilities from triggering, such as that of Chalice of the Void. If one does, its controller puts it on the stack and chooses targets for it, if any. Those abilities will resolve as normal.","oracle_id":"b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Effects that modify a creature’s power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Titanic Growth, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch its power and toughness.","oracle_id":"c0307f8d-b39a-4180-8a45-ddc019ee39f6","published_at":"2016-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gift of Tusks doesn’t counter abilities that have already triggered or been activated. In particular, there is no way to cast this spell to stop a creature’s ability that says “At the beginning of your upkeep,” “When this creature enters the battlefield,” or similar from triggering.","oracle_id":"c0307f8d-b39a-4180-8a45-ddc019ee39f6","published_at":"2016-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gift of Tusks overwrites all previous effects that set the creature’s base power and toughness to specific values. Any power- or toughness-setting effects that start to apply after Gift of Tusks resolves will overwrite this effect.","oracle_id":"c0307f8d-b39a-4180-8a45-ddc019ee39f6","published_at":"2016-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the affected creature gains an ability after Gift of Tusks resolves, it will keep that ability.","oracle_id":"c0307f8d-b39a-4180-8a45-ddc019ee39f6","published_at":"2016-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The creature will lose all other colors and creature types, but it will retain any other card types (such as artifact) or supertypes (such as legendary) it may have.","oracle_id":"c0307f8d-b39a-4180-8a45-ddc019ee39f6","published_at":"2016-01-22","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
